[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2543832693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100144#issuecomment-2543832693","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100144","id":2543832693,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Xn851","user":{"login":"Tetane","id":13542748,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTQyNzQ4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13542748?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane","html_url":"https://github.com/Tetane","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Tetane/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-15T11:17:06Z","updated_at":"2024-12-15T11:17:06Z","body":"The profiler seems to only be displaying functions that are called during the current frame. I made a function that is called every two frame, and when I move frame by frame into the profiler, I can see the function only displayed every two frame.\nMaybe it is not a bug and the profiler is intended to work like that, but when the game is running, functions seems to be appearing and disappearing randomly, which feels like a bug.\nIf the checkbox of a function is set to true in the profiler, maybe it should always be displayed even if it is not called during the current frame?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comme